id: pm-brief-yigc
title: Publication history contains a non-public author identity and requires coordinated rewrite approval
description: "A full git author/committer identity audit found a non-public historical address across published commits. The current tree credential scan is clean apart from intentional fake-token test fixtures, but the public commit graph does not satisfy the privacy release gate. Do not publish a new release or claim full history privacy until a maintainer approves a coordinated history rewrite, retags releases, migrates downstream clones/worktrees, and verifies every ref."
type: Issue
status: canceled
priority: 0
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-07T07:32:45.100Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T07:46:28.106Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T07:46:28.078Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: Maintainer explicitly approves the destructive published-history rewrite plan; every branch and tag is rewritten to public-safe identities without changing tree content; force-updated refs and downstream clone migration are coordinated; post-rewrite author committer tagger and content scans pass across every ref; npm and GitHub release provenance remains documented; the package release gate fails closed until completion
risk: critical
severity: critical
resolution: "Not a release blocker. Companion decision pm-cli-website-ikjv explicitly accepts the personal identities forward-only, and companion epic pm-cli-website-ktip reaffirms that the observed address is one of exactly three approved public identities. The scan found no unapproved address or credential."
expected_result: Only identities outside the companion-approved public allowlist block release.
actual_result: Every observed pm-brief author/committer identity is within the standing approved allowlist; the current-tree scan found no credential leak.
component: release
close_reason: False positive after reconciling the standing companion identity allowlist decision
